# Build context exclusions for infra/gcp/cloud-run/Dockerfile.
# The context is the REPO ROOT, so without this file Docker uploads .venv,
# .git and every local .env to the daemon on every build.
#
# Two reasons this matters, not one:
#   size  — .venv alone is hundreds of MB and is rebuilt inside the image
#           anyway from requirements.txt; sending it is pure waste.
#   leak  — agents/*/.env hold live API keys. A COPY that catches one bakes
#           a credential into a layer that ships to the registry.
#
# Markdown is deliberately NOT excluded: the email agent's skills ARE .md
# files read at runtime (skills/*/SKILL.md, skills/DRAFTING_RULES.md). An
# image without them starts fine and then fails at step 6 with SkillError.
# The few KB of stray README files are not worth that risk.

# --- credentials: never in an image ---------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- VCS and editor ---------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude
.vscode
.vscode-shared

# --- local Python environments and artefacts --------------------------
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache

# --- runtime state: never bake it into an image ------------------------
# agents/email/.runstate holds live run records — lead email addresses,
# HubSpot contact ids, subject lines. It is git-ignored, so it is invisible
# in a diff but very much present in the build context. Baking it in ships
# prospect PII to the registry AND seeds every new instance with a previous
# developer's run state, which step 8 would then try to resolve events
# against.
**/.runstate
**/.logs
**/*_log.jsonl
**/mailgun_sync_state.json

# --- not needed at runtime -------------------------------------------
**/tests
conftest.py
pytest.ini
data
docs
_to_delete
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
# =====================================================================
# Build context exclusions.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The build context is the REPO ROOT (infra/docker-compose.yml uses context: ..),
# because the Dockerfiles reference agents/<component>/... paths. Without
# this file every build packages and uploads the entire repo — including
# the virtualenv, git history, and data/, which holds real lead records.
#
# None of that reaches the image; it is all transmitted as context. This
# keeps builds fast and keeps production data out of the build service.
# =====================================================================

# --- Version control and CI -------------------------------------------
# VCS / IDE
.git
.github
.gitignore

# --- Virtualenvs and Python caches ------------------------------------
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
.pytest_cache
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info

# --- Real lead data: never needed in any image ------------------------
# data/seeds/b2b/output/lead_profiles_decision_makers.json contains 263
# production contacts with names, emails and phone numbers.
data/

# --- Docs, tests and infra: not part of any runtime image -------------
docs/
tests/
infra/
conftest.py
pytest.ini

# --- Secrets: belt and braces -----------------------------------------
# The gateway's HubSpot client secret lives in
# agents/gateway/config/.env. This guarantees no .env can ever enter a
# build context, even by accident. .env.example is kept.
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# --- Local scratch -----------------------------------------------------
*.log
.DS_Store
REMOVE-STRAY-BRANCH.bat
# Python caches & envs
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.venv-linux/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Per-agent secrets & local ADK state — must NOT be baked into images
**/.env
**/.adk/
**/session.db

# Tests & docs not needed at runtime
**/tests/
docs/
evals/
data/
# ...but bake in the 3 synthetic lead_profile seed CSVs the agent reads at runtime
!data/seeds/b2b/employees_with_company_sample.csv
!data/seeds/b2b/employee_contacts_5234.csv
!data/seeds/b2b/companies_clean_734.csv
_to_delete/
